DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/laser-a-conversation-about-po
 et-fernando-pessoa-2339\n\nRegister here: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar
 /register/WN_7lJ8n_2MSmmUPzyjngS5pg#/registration \n\nThe LASERs (Leonardo
  Art Science Evening Rendezvous) are an international program of evening g
 atherings that bring artists and scientists together for informal presenta
 tions and conversation with an audience\, chaired by cultural historian Pi
 ero Scaruffi. This is the online segment of the December LASER and will be
  devoted to a conversation about one of the greatest writers of the 20th c
 entury:\n\n- Richard Zenith (Author) on "Fernando Pessoa: An Experimental 
 Life" at 12pm California time (evening in Europe).\n\nRichard Zenith is an
  acclaimed translator and literary critic\, best known for his numerous En
 glish editions and studies of Fernando Pessoa’s work. In 2021 Zenith pub
 lished the 1\,055-page biography "Pessoa: An Experimental Life"\, which wa
 s a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize.\n\nBesides Pessoa\, some other outsta
 nding translations include: the medieval anthology "113 Galician-Portugues
 e Troubadour Poems" (1995)\; "Education by Stone: Selected Poems of João 
 Cabral de Melo Neto"(Archipelago\, 2005)\, which won the 2006 translation 
 award from the Academy of American Poets\; "Multitudinous Heart" (2015) a 
 comprehensive collection of poems by Brazilian writer Carlos Drummond de A
 ndrade.\n\nDetailed bio at: Leonardo Art Science Evening Rendezvous LASER\
 n\nThe Stanford LASERs are co-sponsored by the deans of Humanities and Sci
 ences\, Engineering and Medicine\, and by Chemical Engineering.
END:VEVENT
